# A work-tracker id in a reply opens the tracker.
#
# "Built the config diff D948120 adding Tier 1/2/3 price points" — the id is a
# reference to something that lives elsewhere, and it used to be prose. It is
# now drawn as a link and a press on it opens the configured tracker.
#
# THIS SCRIPT USED TO PIN THE PIXEL, and that is the whole reason it has a
# reputation. The id is a byte range inside one wrapped label, not an element,
# so there is no name to click (afterhours_gaps.md #51 — nothing will say
# where a byte range landed), and the script clicked the centre of the rect a
# re-derivation produced at 1100x760. A pinned pixel is a coordinate that
# rots. It rotted twice:
#
#   y=465 -> 144   the pane lost its title header and its short-thread bottom
#                  anchor, which put this line 321px higher.
#   y=147 -> 173   the six feature branches of 2026-08-26 moved every
#                  transcript body line down 26px. perf/post-merge re-measured
#                  select_word_and_line.e2e and
#                  a_click_on_a_line_seam_is_one_click.e2e for that move and
#                  did not reach this script, so it went on failing — alone
#                  AND in the full suite — and was read as a flake for three
#                  sessions. One agent ran it 148 times looking for a race.
#
# So it no longer pins anything. `click_link` (src/ecs/e2e_commands.h) presses
# the centre of the rect the RENDERER derived for that id this frame, which is
# the same rect the hit test tests against, so the two cannot disagree and the
# layout can move as often as it likes. When the id is not on screen at all
# the failure names the links that were, instead of reporting a miss on empty
# space.
#
# `require_thread` states this script's precondition where a reader can see
# it. The `# settings:` line below ASKS for t1; that line is a request, and
# until this command existed nothing checked that it was granted — a script
# whose thread never opened asserted against the sidebar and failed with
# "text not found", which is what three separate investigations chased.
#
# The browser is never launched: a headless render has nobody to hand it to,
# so the open is recorded and the transcript's own confirmation is what is
# asserted here (src/ui/link_detect.h).
#
# HANABI_LINK_AUDIT=1 still prints every rect the hit test tested, and is
# still the way to see where a link landed.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t1"],"active_tab":"t1","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_TRACKER_BASE_URL=https://tracker.example.com HANABI_LINK_AUDIT=1

require_thread t1
expect_text "Built the config diff"

click_link D948120
wait_frames 10
expect_text "Opened D948120"
